## Why this repair

The failed judgement is the then step `the calculator prints 3`, which reached only 7 against
concept `then / result` (threshold 9). The reason given is not a missing item and not a new kind
of use: `result` is already the right Public interface item (what the calculator prints) and
already the right kind of use (printing the computed whole number). It scores short only because
its `means` is worded closed to one variation — "the whole number the **doubling** produced" — so
printing the **halving**'s output is an unstated variation of the same item and use.

Therefore the repair widens the existing concept `result` rather than adding a concept, and does
not rewrite the Story. The widening is done by rewriting `means` into closed prose that states
every variation the concept admits — the product has exactly two computing operations, `doubling`
and `halving`, so both are named and the prose admits nothing further.

This also repairs the earlier rejected attempt, which declared the variations under a separate
`variations:` key and left the document unreadable. A concept holds only `concept`, `means` and
`terms`; the variations belong inside `means`. No new key is introduced here.

